  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Los verbos en -er",
    "@en": "The verbs in -er"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "La mayoría de los verbos franceses acaban en **-er**. Los regulares, como **parler** (hablar), **habiter** (vivir) y **travailler** (trabajar), siguen el mismo modelo; **aller** (ir) es una excepción irregular frecuente.",
     "@en": "Most French verbs end up in **-er**. Regular ones, such as **parler** (talk), **habiter** (live) and **travailler** (work), follow the same model; **aller** (go) is a frequent irregular exception."
    },
    {
     "@es": "En los verbos regulares, se quita **-er** y se añaden las terminaciones: **-e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent**.",
     "@en": "In the regular verbs, **-er** is removed and the endings are added: **-e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Lo importante al hablar: **je parle, tu parles, il parle** e **ils parlent** suenan **exactamente igual** («parl»). Solo se oyen distintas **nous parlons** y **vous parlez**.",
     "@en": "The important thing when speaking: **je parle, tu parles, il parle** and **ils parlent** sound **exactamente igual** («parl»). Only different **nous parlons** and **vous parlez** are heard."
    }
   ]
  },
